IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc20-part16-notices.l4 -- sections 500 to 502.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada): the contents of an appearance notice and of an undertaking, the variation of an undertaking, and how the accused
-- appears. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); a duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE.
-- A requirement that a document "shall" or "must" contain something is encoded as "the document meets the requirement": JUST TRUE when every element is present, JUST FALSE when one the text requires is missing.

§ `Section 500 -- Contents of an appearance notice`

-- src:11144 | Contents of appearance notice
-- src:11145 | 500 (1) An appearance notice shall
-- src:11146 | (a) set out the name, date of birth and contact information of the accused;
-- src:11147 | (b) set out the substance of the offence that the accused is alleged to have committed;
-- src:11148 | (c) require the accused to attend court at a time and place to be stated in the notice and to attend afterwards as required by the court; and
-- src:11149 | (d) indicate if the accused is required to appear at a judicial referral hearing under section 523.1 for a failure under section 496.
@ref s 500(1) (src:11144-11149)
GIVEN `the notice sets out the name, date of birth and contact information of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice sets out the substance of the offence that the accused is alleged to have committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires the accused to attend court at a time and place stated in it and to attend afterwards as required by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is required to appear at a judicial referral hearing under section 523.1 for a failure under section 496` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice indicates that the accused is required to appear at a judicial referral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(1) the appearance notice meets the requirements of paragraphs (a) to (d)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the notice sets out the name, date of birth and contact information of the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appearance notice shall (a) set out the name, date of birth and contact information of the accused"
        IF NOT `the notice sets out the substance of the offence that the accused is alleged to have committed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) set out the substance of the offence that the accused is alleged to have committed"
        IF NOT `the notice requires the accused to attend court at a time and place stated in it and to attend afterwards as required by the court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) require the accused to attend court at a time and place to be stated in the notice"
        IF `the accused is required to appear at a judicial referral hearing under section 523.1 for a failure under section 496` AND NOT `the notice indicates that the accused is required to appear at a judicial referral hearing`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) indicate if the accused is required to appear at a judicial referral hearing under section 523.1 for a failure under section 496"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11150 | Summary of consequences — failure to appear
-- src:11151 | (2) An appearance notice shall set out a summary of subsections 145(3) and (6), section 512.2 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2) and the possible consequences of a failure to appear at a judicial referral hearing under section 523.1.
@ref s 500(2) (src:11150-11151)
GIVEN `the notice sets out a summary of subsections 145(3) and (6), section 512.2 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2) and the possible consequences of a failure to appear at a judicial referral hearing under section 523.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(2) the appearance notice sets out the required summary` MEANS
    IF `the notice sets out a summary of subsections 145(3) and (6), section 512.2 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2) and the possible consequences of a failure to appear at a judicial referral hearing under section 523.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appearance notice shall set out a summary of subsections 145(3) and (6), section 512.2 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)"

-- src:11152 | Attendance for purposes of Identification of Criminals Act
-- src:11153 | (3) An appearance notice may require the accused to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, if the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act.
@ref s 500(3) (src:11152-11153)
GIVEN `the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(3) the appearance notice may require the accused to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` MEANS
    IF `the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails; the Identification of Criminals Act is outside the sources)

-- src:11154 | Signature of accused
-- src:11155 | (4) An accused shall be requested to sign in duplicate their appearance notice and, whether or not they comply with that request, one of the duplicates shall be given to the accused. If the accused fails or refuses to sign, the lack of their signature does not invalidate the appearance notice.
@ref s 500(4) (src:11154-11155)
GIVEN `the accused was requested to sign the appearance notice in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the duplicates was given to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(4) the officer has done what subsection (4) requires about the signature` MEANS
    IF `the accused was requested to sign the appearance notice in duplicate` AND `one of the duplicates was given to the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An accused shall be requested to sign in duplicate their appearance notice and, whether or not they comply with that request, one of the duplicates shall be given to the accused"

@ref s 500(4) (src:11155)
GIVEN `the accused fails or refuses to sign` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 500(4) the lack of the accused's signature invalidates the appearance notice` MEANS
    IF `the accused fails or refuses to sign`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the lack of their signature does not invalidate the appearance notice"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence is about an accused who fails or refuses to sign; where the accused signed there is no lack of signature to speak of

§ `Section 501 -- Contents of an undertaking`

-- src:11156 | Contents of undertaking
-- src:11157 | 501 (1) An undertaking under paragraph 498(1)(c), 499(b) or 503(1.1)(b) must set out
-- src:11158 | (a) the name, date of birth and contact information of the accused;
-- src:11159 | (b) the substance of the offence that the accused is alleged to have committed; and
-- src:11160 | (c) a summary of subsections 145(4) and (6), sections 512 and 512.2 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2).
@ref s 501(1) (src:11156-11160)
GIVEN `the undertaking is one given under paragraph 498(1)(c), 499(b) or 503(1.1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking sets out the name, date of birth and contact information of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking sets out the substance of the offence that the accused is alleged to have committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking sets out a summary of subsections 145(4) and (6), sections 512 and 512.2 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(1) the undertaking sets out the required contents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the undertaking is one given under paragraph 498(1)(c), 499(b) or 503(1.1)(b)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An undertaking under paragraph 498(1)(c), 499(b) or 503(1.1)(b) must set out"
        IF `the undertaking sets out the name, date of birth and contact information of the accused`
           AND `the undertaking sets out the substance of the offence that the accused is alleged to have committed`
           AND `the undertaking sets out a summary of subsections 145(4) and (6), sections 512 and 512.2 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must set out (a) the name, date of birth and contact information of the accused; (b) the substance of the offence ...; and (c) a summary of subsections 145(4) and (6)"

-- src:11161 | Mandatory conditions
-- src:11162 | (2) The undertaking must contain a condition that the accused attend court at the time and place stated in the undertaking and to attend afterwards as required by the court.
@ref s 501(2) (src:11161-11162)
GIVEN `the undertaking contains a condition that the accused attend court at the time and place stated in the undertaking and afterwards as required by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(2) the undertaking contains the mandatory condition` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking contains a condition that the accused attend court at the time and place stated in the undertaking and afterwards as required by the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The undertaking must contain a condition that the accused attend court at the time and place stated in the undertaking"

-- 501(3): the conditions an undertaking may contain, one constructor for each of paragraphs (a) to (k), and one for a condition the list does not name.
-- src:11163 | Additional conditions
-- src:11164 | (3) The undertaking may contain one or more of the following conditions, if the condition is reasonable in the circumstances of the offence and necessary, to ensure the accused’s attendance in court or the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence, or to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence:
-- src:11165 | (a) report at specified times to the peace officer or other specified person;
-- src:11166 | (b) remain within a specified territorial jurisdiction;
-- src:11167 | (c) notify the peace officer or other specified person of any change in their address, employment or occupation;
-- src:11168 | (d) abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the undertaking, except in accordance with any specified conditions;
-- src:11169 | (e) abstain from going to any specified place or entering any geographic area related to any person referred to in paragraph (d), except in accordance with any specified conditions;
-- src:11170 | (f) deposit all their passports with the peace officer or other specified person;
-- src:11171 | (g) reside at a specified address, be at that address at specified hours and present themselves at the entrance of that residence to a peace officer or other specified person, at the officer’s or specified person’s request during those hours;
-- src:11172 | (h) abstain from possessing a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, and surrender those that are in their possession to the peace officer or other specified person and also any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling them to acquire or possess them;
-- src:11173 | (i) promise to pay an amount specified in the undertaking, which shall not be more than $500, if they fail to comply with any condition of the undertaking;
-- src:11174 | (j) deposit, with the peace officer specified in the undertaking, money or other valuable security whose value does not exceed $500 if, at the time of giving the undertaking, the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres of the place in which they are in custody; and
-- src:11175 | (k) comply with any other specified condition for ensuring the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence.
@ref s 501(3) (src:11163-11175)
DECLARE `s 501(3) the condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 501(3)(a) report at specified times to the peace officer or other specified person`
    `s 501(3)(b) remain within a specified territorial jurisdiction`
    `s 501(3)(c) notify the peace officer or other specified person of any change in address, employment or occupation`
    `s 501(3)(d) abstain from communicating with any victim, witness or other person identified in the undertaking`
    `s 501(3)(e) abstain from going to any specified place or entering any geographic area related to any person referred to in paragraph (d)`
    `s 501(3)(f) deposit all passports with the peace officer or other specified person`
    `s 501(3)(g) reside at a specified address, be at that address at specified hours and present themselves to a peace officer or other specified person`
    `s 501(3)(h) abstain from possessing a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, and surrender them and any authorization, licence or registration certificate`
    `s 501(3)(i) promise to pay an amount specified in the undertaking`
    `s 501(3)(j) deposit money or other valuable security`
    `s 501(3)(k) comply with any other specified condition for ensuring the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence`
    `s 501(3) a condition the list does not name`

@ref s 501(3) (src:11163-11175)
GIVEN condition IS A `s 501(3) the condition`
      `the condition is reasonable in the circumstances of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is necessary to ensure the accused's attendance in court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is necessary to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of money or value of security, in dollars (0 if the condition has no amount)` IS A NUMBER
      `the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres of the place in which they are in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(3) the undertaking may contain the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF condition EQUALS `s 501(3) a condition the list does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The undertaking may contain one or more of the following conditions" (the list does not say "only")
        IF condition EQUALS `s 501(3)(i) promise to pay an amount specified in the undertaking` AND `the amount of money or value of security, in dollars (0 if the condition has no amount)` GREATER THAN 500
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) promise to pay an amount specified in the undertaking, which shall not be more than $500"
        IF condition EQUALS `s 501(3)(j) deposit money or other valuable security` AND `the amount of money or value of security, in dollars (0 if the condition has no amount)` GREATER THAN 500
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(j) deposit, with the peace officer specified in the undertaking, money or other valuable security whose value does not exceed $500"
        IF NOT (`the condition is reasonable in the circumstances of the offence`
                AND (   `the condition is necessary to ensure the accused's attendance in court`
                     OR `the condition is necessary to ensure the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence`
                     OR `the condition is necessary to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence`))
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the condition is reasonable in the circumstances of the offence and necessary, to ensure the accused’s attendance in court or the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence, or to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)
        IF condition EQUALS `s 501(3)(j) deposit money or other valuable security` AND NOT `the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres of the place in which they are in custody`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(j) ... if, at the time of giving the undertaking, the accused is not ordinarily resident in the province or does not ordinarily reside within 200 kilometres of the place in which they are in custody" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11176 | Attendance for purposes of Identification of Criminals Act
-- src:11177 | (4) The undertaking may require the accused to appear at the time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, if the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act.
@ref s 501(4) (src:11176-11177)
GIVEN `the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(4) the undertaking may require the accused to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` MEANS
    IF `the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is alleged to have committed an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails; the Identification of Criminals Act is outside the sources)

-- src:11178 | Money or other valuable security to be deposited with justice
-- src:11179 | (5) If the accused has deposited an amount of money or other valuable security with a peace officer, the officer shall, without delay after the deposit, cause the money or valuable security to be delivered to a justice for deposit with the justice.
@ref s 501(5) (src:11178-11179)
GIVEN `the accused has deposited an amount of money or other valuable security with a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has caused the money or valuable security to be delivered to a justice for deposit, without delay after the deposit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(5) the officer has delivered the deposit to a justice as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused has deposited an amount of money or other valuable security with a peace officer` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused has deposited an amount of money or other valuable security with a peace officer, the officer shall"
        IF `the officer has caused the money or valuable security to be delivered to a justice for deposit, without delay after the deposit` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the officer shall, without delay after the deposit, cause the money or valuable security to be delivered to a justice for deposit with the justice"

-- src:11180 | Signature of accused
-- src:11181 | (6) The accused shall be requested to sign in duplicate their undertaking and, whether or not they comply with that request, one of the duplicates shall be given to them. If they fail or refuse to sign, the lack of their signature does not invalidate the undertaking.
@ref s 501(6) (src:11180-11181)
GIVEN `the accused was requested to sign the undertaking in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the duplicates was given to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(6) the officer has done what subsection (6) requires about the signature` MEANS
    IF `the accused was requested to sign the undertaking in duplicate` AND `one of the duplicates was given to the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The accused shall be requested to sign in duplicate their undertaking and, whether or not they comply with that request, one of the duplicates shall be given to them"

@ref s 501(6) (src:11181)
GIVEN `the accused fails or refuses to sign` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 501(6) the lack of the accused's signature invalidates the undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the accused fails or refuses to sign`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the lack of their signature does not invalidate the undertaking"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence is about an accused who fails or refuses to sign

§ `Section 502 -- Variation of an undertaking`

-- src:11182 | Variation of undertaking on consent
-- src:11183 | 502 (1) The undertaking in respect of which an accused has been released under section 498, 499 or 503 may, with the written consent of the accused and the prosecutor, be varied and the undertaking so varied is deemed to be an undertaking given under section 498, 499 or 503, as the case may be.
@ref s 502(1) (src:11182-11183)
GIVEN `the accused was released on an undertaking under section 498, 499 or 503` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents in writing to the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents in writing to the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502(1) the undertaking may be varied` MEANS
    IF `the accused was released on an undertaking under section 498, 499 or 503` AND `the accused consents in writing to the variation` AND `the prosecutor consents in writing to the variation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with the written consent of the accused and the prosecutor, be varied" (a "may" whose gate fails)

@ref s 502(1) and (2)(b) the varied undertaking is deemed (src:11183)
GIVEN `the undertaking was varied under subsection (1) or paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502 the varied undertaking is deemed to be an undertaking given under section 498, 499 or 503` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking was varied under subsection (1) or paragraph (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the deeming is for "the undertaking so varied"; the text says nothing of an undertaking not varied under those provisions

-- src:11184 | Replacement or variation without consent
-- src:11185 | (2) The accused or the prosecutor may, in the absence of consent between them,
-- src:11186 | (a) apply to a justice for a release order referred to in section 515 to replace an undertaking given by the accused under paragraph 498(1)(c), 499(b) or 503(1.1)(b) with the order; or
-- src:11187 | (b) apply to a justice to vary the undertaking in respect of which the accused has been released under section 498, 499 or 503, in which case the undertaking so varied is deemed to be an undertaking given under section 498, 499 or 503, as the case may be.
-- src:11188 | If the prosecutor makes the application, the prosecutor must provide three days’ notice to the accused.
@ref s 502(2) (src:11184-11188)
GIVEN `there is no consent between the accused and the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is to replace an undertaking given under paragraph 498(1)(c), 499(b) or 503(1.1)(b) with a release order referred to in section 515` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is to vary the undertaking in respect of which the accused has been released under section 498, 499 or 503` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502(2) the accused or the prosecutor may apply to a justice` MEANS
    IF `there is no consent between the accused and the prosecutor`
       AND (`the application is to replace an undertaking given under paragraph 498(1)(c), 499(b) or 503(1.1)(b) with a release order referred to in section 515`   -- (a)
            OR `the application is to vary the undertaking in respect of which the accused has been released under section 498, 499 or 503`)   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, in the absence of consent between them, (a) apply to a justice ...; or (b) apply to a justice to vary the undertaking" (a "may" whose gate fails; "in the absence of consent" is read like the "with consent" gates of ss 502(1), 503(3.1), 519.1 and 523(2)(c), as an "if"-type gate; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

@ref s 502(2) the last sentence (src:11188)
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days of notice the prosecutor gave the accused` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502(2) the prosecutor's notice to the accused of three days is given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor makes the application` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence "If the prosecutor makes the application, the prosecutor must provide three days’ notice to the accused" states no notice for an application the accused makes
        IF `the days of notice the prosecutor gave the accused` AT LEAST 3 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the prosecutor must provide three days’ notice to the accused"

§ `Section 502.1 -- Appearance of the accused, witnesses, participants and the justice`

-- src:11192 | 502.1 (1) Except as otherwise provided in this Part, an accused who is required to appear in a proceeding under this Part shall appear in person but may appear by audioconference or videoconference, if arrangements are made with the court in advance and those arrangements are satisfactory to the justice.
@ref s 502.1(1) (src:11192)
GIVEN `this Part provides otherwise for the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502.1(1) the accused must appear in person` MEANS
    IF `this Part provides otherwise for the proceeding`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as otherwise provided in this Part, an accused who is required to appear in a proceeding under this Part shall appear in person"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 502.1(1) (src:11192)
GIVEN `arrangements are made with the court in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those arrangements are satisfactory to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502.1(1) the accused may appear by audioconference or videoconference` MEANS
    IF `arrangements are made with the court in advance` AND `those arrangements are satisfactory to the justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may appear by audioconference or videoconference, if arrangements are made with the court in advance and those arrangements are satisfactory to the justice" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11193 | Witness in Canada
-- src:11194 | (2) Despite section 714.1, a witness in Canada who is required to give evidence in a proceeding under this Part may do so by audioconference or videoconference, if it is satisfactory to the justice.
@ref s 502.1(2) (src:11193-11194)
GIVEN `the witness is in Canada and required to give evidence in a proceeding under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is satisfactory to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502.1(2) the witness in Canada may give evidence by audioconference or videoconference` MEANS
    IF `the witness is in Canada and required to give evidence in a proceeding under this Part` AND `it is satisfactory to the justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may do so by audioconference or videoconference, if it is satisfactory to the justice" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11195 | Witness outside Canada
-- src:11196 | (3) For greater certainty, sections 714.2 to 714.8 apply when a witness outside Canada gives evidence in a proceeding under this Part.
@ref s 502.1(3) (src:11195-11196)
GIVEN `the witness is outside Canada and gives evidence in a proceeding under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502.1(3) sections 714.2 to 714.8 apply` MEANS
    IF `the witness is outside Canada and gives evidence in a proceeding under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when sections 714.2 to 714.8 apply; it does not say they do not apply otherwise

-- src:11197 | Participants
-- src:11198 | (4) A participant, as defined in subsection 715.25(1), who is to participate in a proceeding under this Part shall participate in person but may participate by audioconference or videoconference, if it is satisfactory to the justice.
@ref s 502.1(4) (src:11197-11198)
GIVEN `s 715.25 the person is a participant as defined in subsection 715.25(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is satisfactory to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502.1(4) the participant may participate by audioconference or videoconference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 715.25 the person is a participant as defined in subsection 715.25(1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "A participant, as defined in subsection 715.25(1)" (section 715.25 is outside this range)
        IF `s 715.25 the person is a participant as defined in subsection 715.25(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A participant, as defined in subsection 715.25(1), who is to participate in a proceeding under this Part ... may participate" (a "may" for participants only)
        IF `it is satisfactory to the justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may participate by audioconference or videoconference, if it is satisfactory to the justice" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11199 | Justice
-- src:11200 | (5) The justice who is to preside at a proceeding under this Part shall preside in person but may preside by audioconference or videoconference, if the justice considers it necessary in the circumstances.
@ref s 502.1(5) (src:11199-11200)
GIVEN `the justice considers it necessary in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 502.1(5) the justice may preside by audioconference or videoconference` MEANS
    IF `the justice considers it necessary in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may preside by audioconference or videoconference, if the justice considers it necessary in the circumstances" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)
